</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 4.5 (Convergence of Quantized Adam). ‣ 4.1 Theoretical results of Adam ‣ 4 Main Results ‣ A Convergence Analysis of Adaptive Optimizers under Floating-point Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a></h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Preliminaries</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider an optimization problem in a <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional space (let <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=mn" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=mn</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of trainable parameters), where coordinates are indexed by <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[d]=\{1,2,\ldots,d\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[d]=\{1,2,\ldots,d\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Our algorithm generates a sequence of vectors <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{u}_{t})_{t\in\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{u}_{t})_{t\in\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math>, with the <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th component of <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> denoted by <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t,i}</annotation></semantics></math>. The objective is to find a critical point of a global function <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> within a stochastic framework, where we have access to a sequence of i.i.d. sample functions <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f_{t})_{t\in\mathbb{N}^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f_{t})_{t\in\mathbb{N}^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., the loss on a data minibatch). For any differentiable function <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, we denote its gradient by <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla h</annotation></semantics></math> and its <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th component by <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{i}h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{i}h</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, we use a small constant <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for numerical stability and let <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{t}[\cdot]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{t}[\cdot]</annotation></semantics></math> denote the conditional expectation given the history of samples <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{1},\ldots,f_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{1},\ldots,f_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. We use <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{vec}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{vec}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> to vectorize a matrix and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{mat}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>mat</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{mat}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> for the inverse operation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Recall the dynamic system of our theoretical Quantized Adam. In the proof, we denote <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}_{t}=\mathrm{vec}(\mathbf{W}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}_{t}=\mathrm{vec}(\mathbf{W}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{g}_{t}}=\mathrm{vec}(\mathbf{G}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐆</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{g}_{t}}=\mathrm{vec}(\mathbf{G}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and the dimension <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=m\cdot n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=m\cdot n</annotation></semantics></math>. For an iteration <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\mathbb{N}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\mathbb{N}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{cases}m_{t,i}&amp;=\beta_{1}m_{t-1,i}^{Q}+\hat{g}_{t,i}=\beta_{1}(m_{t-1,i}+\xi_{t-1,i})+(\nabla_{i}f_{t}(\mathbf{w}_{t-1})+\delta_{t,i}),\\
v_{t,i}&amp;=\beta_{2}v_{t-1,i}^{Q}+\hat{g}_{t,i}^{2}=\beta_{2}(v_{t-1,i}+\theta_{t-1,i})+\left(\nabla_{i}f_{t}(\mathbf{w}_{t-1})+\delta_{t,i}\right)^{2},\\
w_{t,i}&amp;=w_{t-1,i}-\eta_{t}\frac{m_{t,i}}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v_{t,i}}}.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>Q</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>Q</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msqrt><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{cases}m_{t,i}&amp;=\beta_{1}m_{t-1,i}^{Q}+\hat{g}_{t,i}=\beta_{1}(m_{t-1,i}+\xi_{t-1,i})+(\nabla_{i}f_{t}(\mathbf{w}_{t-1})+\delta_{t,i}),\\
v_{t,i}&amp;=\beta_{2}v_{t-1,i}^{Q}+\hat{g}_{t,i}^{2}=\beta_{2}(v_{t-1,i}+\theta_{t-1,i})+\left(\nabla_{i}f_{t}(\mathbf{w}_{t-1})+\delta_{t,i}\right)^{2},\\
w_{t,i}&amp;=w_{t-1,i}-\eta_{t}\frac{m_{t,i}}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v_{t,i}}}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">with the step size given by</p>
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eta_{t}=\eta(1-\beta_{1})\sqrt{\frac{1-\beta_{2}^{t}}{1-\beta_{2}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta_{t}=\eta(1-\beta_{1})\sqrt{\frac{1-\beta_{2}^{t}}{1-\beta_{2}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{t,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{t,i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{t-1,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{t-1,i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t-1,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t-1,i}</annotation></semantics></math> represent the quantization errors for the gradient, first moment, and second moment, respectively. Especially,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{i}f_{t}(\mathbf{w}_{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{i}f_{t}(\mathbf{w}_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{B}\sum_{j=1}^{B}\nabla_{i}f(\mathbf{w}_{t-1};\gamma_{t,j})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{B}\sum_{j=1}^{B}\nabla_{i}f(\mathbf{w}_{t-1};\gamma_{t,j}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\delta_{t,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\delta_{t,i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{B}\sum_{j=1}^{B}\nabla_{i}^{Q}f(\mathbf{w}_{t-1}^{Q};\gamma_{t,j})-\frac{1}{B}\sum_{j=1}^{B}\nabla_{i}f_{t}(\mathbf{w}_{t-1};\gamma_{t,j})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{B}\sum_{j=1}^{B}\nabla_{i}^{Q}f(\mathbf{w}_{t-1}^{Q};\gamma_{t,j})-\frac{1}{B}\sum_{j=1}^{B}\nabla_{i}f_{t}(\mathbf{w}_{t-1};\gamma_{t,j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">We have <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\nabla_{i}f_{t}(\mathbf{w}_{t-1})\right]=\nabla_{i}F(\mathbf{w}_{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\nabla_{i}f_{t}(\mathbf{w}_{t-1})\right]=\nabla_{i}F(\mathbf{w}_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Our convergence analysis for Quantized Adam is predicated on a specific, analytically convenient formulation of the algorithm. This section serves to rigorously justify our theoretical framework by establishing two foundational equivalences. First, we demonstrate that our representation of the Adam update is equivalent to the standard formulation. Following the methodology of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Défossez et al. [2022]</a></cite>, we absorb the scaling factor into the learning rate, which simplifies the recursive structure of the momentum term. Second, and more critically for our work, we prove that the theoretical analysis of quantizing these weighted-sum states is directly applicable to the practical scenario of quantizing the standard weighted-average states.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Equivalence with Standard Adam</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our formulation in (<a href="#A1.E1" title="In A.1 Preliminaries ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem ‣ A Convergence Analysis of Adaptive Optimizers under Floating-point Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>) utilizes a weighted sum for the moments, which differs slightly from the standard weighted-average approach in the original Adam algorithm <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kingma, 2014</a>]</cite>. The standard first moment, often expressed as <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{m}_{t,i}=(1-\beta_{1})\sum_{k=1}^{t}\beta_{1}^{t-k}\hat{g}_{k,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{m}_{t,i}=(1-\beta_{1})\sum_{k=1}^{t}\beta_{1}^{t-k}\hat{g}_{k,i}</annotation></semantics></math>, is simply a scaled version of our definition, i.e., <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{m}_{t,i}=(1-\beta_{1})m_{t,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{m}_{t,i}=(1-\beta_{1})m_{t,i}</annotation></semantics></math>. This constant scaling factor can be directly absorbed into the learning rate.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Furthermore, the standard Adam algorithm includes bias correction terms to counteract the zero-initialization of moments. These corrections are equivalent to using a time-dependent step size of the form:</p>
<table id="A1.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{t,\text{Adam}}=\eta\cdot\frac{1-\beta_{1}}{\sqrt{1-\beta_{2}}}\cdot\frac{\sqrt{1-\beta_{2}^{t}}}{1-\beta_{1}^{t}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Adam</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{t,\text{Adam}}=\eta\cdot\frac{1-\beta_{1}}{\sqrt{1-\beta_{2}}}\cdot\frac{\sqrt{1-\beta_{2}^{t}}}{1-\beta_{1}^{t}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">For analytical tractability, our analysis adopts the simplified step size <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> from (<a href="#A1.E2" title="In A.1 Preliminaries ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem ‣ A Convergence Analysis of Adaptive Optimizers under Floating-point Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>), which omits the bias correction for the first moment (<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{t,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{t,i}</annotation></semantics></math>). This simplification is motivated by several practical and theoretical considerations. First, it ensures that our step size <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is monotonic with respect to <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, which is advantageous for the convergence proof. Second, for typical hyperparameter values (e.g., <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}=0.999" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.999</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}=0.999</annotation></semantics></math>), the omitted term <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/(1-\beta_{1}^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/(1-\beta_{1}^{t})</annotation></semantics></math> converges to its limit of 1 much more rapidly than the retained term <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{1-\beta_{2}^{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{1-\beta_{2}^{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, removing this term effectively implements a learning rate warm-up, a common and beneficial practice, while retaining the correction for <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t,i}</annotation></semantics></math> prevents an undesirably large initial step size that could lead to training instability.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Equivalence of Quantization Schemes.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A subtle but crucial aspect of our setup is the object of quantization. Our theoretical framework analyzes the quantization of weighted-sum moments (<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{m}_{t},\mathbf{v}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{m}_{t},\mathbf{v}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>), while a practical implementation would quantize the standard weighted-average moments (<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{m}}_{t},\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{m}}_{t},\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>). We now prove that these two approaches are, in fact, analytically equivalent.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To establish this rigorously, we first abstract the core dynamic behavior into a general mathematical lemma. We will show that two discrete-time systems, representing the weighted-sum and weighted-average accumulation methods under relative error perturbations, are analytically indistinguishable. We will then apply this result to the specific case of Quantized Adam.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Equivalence of Perturbed Dynamical Systems)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider two scalar sequences <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{a_{k}\}_{k\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{a_{k}\}_{k\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{c_{k}\}_{k\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{c_{k}\}_{k\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> evolving according to the following dynamics for <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, with initial conditions <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{0}=c_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{0}=c_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta(a_{k-1}+d_{k-1})+b_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta(a_{k-1}+d_{k-1})+b_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta(c_{k-1}+e_{k-1})+(1-\beta)b_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta(c_{k-1}+e_{k-1})+(1-\beta)b_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> is a decay factor, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{b_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{b_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is an external input sequence, and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{d_{k}\},\{e_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{d_{k}\},\{e_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> are perturbation sequences. These perturbations are bounded by a relative error model with factor <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in[0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in[0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|d_{k-1}|\leq q|a_{k-1}|\quad\text{and}\quad|e_{k-1}|\leq q|c_{k-1}|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|d_{k-1}|\leq q|a_{k-1}|\quad\text{and}\quad|e_{k-1}|\leq q|c_{k-1}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, the sequence <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{c_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{c_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and the scaled sequence <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{a^{\prime}_{k}\}\triangleq(1-\beta)a_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{a^{\prime}_{k}\}\triangleq(1-\beta)a_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> are analytically equivalent. Specifically, they follow identical recurrence relations where their respective perturbation terms satisfy identical relative error bounds with respect to their own states.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">To prove the equivalence, we derive the recurrence relation for the scaled sequence <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{a^{\prime}_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{a^{\prime}_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and compare its structure and error properties to that of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{c_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{c_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1: Derive the recurrence for <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{a^{\prime}_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{a^{\prime}_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Starting from the definition <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{\prime}_{k}=(1-\beta)a_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\prime}_{k}=(1-\beta)a_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and substituting the dynamics from (<a href="#A1.E4" title="In Lemma A.1 (Equivalence of Perturbed Dynamical Systems). ‣ Equivalence of Quantization Schemes. ‣ A.1 Preliminaries ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem ‣ A Convergence Analysis of Adaptive Optimizers under Floating-point Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>):</span></span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a^{\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a^{\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\beta)\left[\beta(a_{k-1}+d_{k-1})+b_{k}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\beta)\left[\beta(a_{k-1}+d_{k-1})+b_{k}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta(1-\beta)a_{k-1}+\beta(1-\beta)d_{k-1}+(1-\beta)b_{k}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta(1-\beta)a_{k-1}+\beta(1-\beta)d_{k-1}+(1-\beta)b_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Now, we replace <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{\prime}_{k-1}/(1-\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\prime}_{k-1}/(1-\beta)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a^{\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a^{\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta(1-\beta)\left(\frac{a^{\prime}_{k-1}}{1-\beta}\right)+\beta(1-\beta)d_{k-1}+(1-\beta)b_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta(1-\beta)\left(\frac{a^{\prime}_{k-1}}{1-\beta}\right)+\beta(1-\beta)d_{k-1}+(1-\beta)b_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta a^{\prime}_{k-1}+\beta(1-\beta)d_{k-1}+(1-\beta)b_{k}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta a^{\prime}_{k-1}+\beta(1-\beta)d_{k-1}+(1-\beta)b_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2: Compare recurrence structures.<span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Let us place the recurrence relations for <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{c_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{c_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{a^{\prime}_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{a^{\prime}_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> side-by-side:</span></span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta c_{k-1}+\beta e_{k-1}+(1-\beta)b_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta c_{k-1}+\beta e_{k-1}+(1-\beta)b_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a^{\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a^{\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta a^{\prime}_{k-1}+\beta(1-\beta)d_{k-1}+(1-\beta)b_{k}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta a^{\prime}_{k-1}+\beta(1-\beta)d_{k-1}+(1-\beta)b_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Both sequences share the identical structure: <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{k}=\beta X_{k-1}+\text{Perturbation}_{k}+(1-\beta)b_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mtext>Perturbation</mtext><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{k}=\beta X_{k-1}+\text{Perturbation}_{k}+(1-\beta)b_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. The only difference lies in the form of their respective perturbation terms.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3: Compare relative bounds of the perturbation terms.<span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
The equivalence hinges on whether these different perturbation terms satisfy the same relative error property with respect to their own system’s state.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">For system <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{c_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{c_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the perturbation term is <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta e_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta e_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using the bound from (<a href="#A1.E6" title="In Lemma A.1 (Equivalence of Perturbed Dynamical Systems). ‣ Equivalence of Quantization Schemes. ‣ A.1 Preliminaries ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem ‣ A Convergence Analysis of Adaptive Optimizers under Floating-point Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\text{Perturbation}_{c}|=|\beta e_{k-1}|=\beta|e_{k-1}|\leq\beta q|c_{k-1}|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mtext>Perturbation</mtext><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\text{Perturbation}_{c}|=|\beta e_{k-1}|=\beta|e_{k-1}|\leq\beta q|c_{k-1}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">For system <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{a^{\prime}_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{a^{\prime}_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the effective perturbation term is <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(1-\beta)d_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(1-\beta)d_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using the bound from (<a href="#A1.E6" title="In Lemma A.1 (Equivalence of Perturbed Dynamical Systems). ‣ Equivalence of Quantization Schemes. ‣ A.1 Preliminaries ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem ‣ A Convergence Analysis of Adaptive Optimizers under Floating-point Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a>) and the scaling relationship <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{k-1}=a^{\prime}_{k-1}/(1-\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{k-1}=a^{\prime}_{k-1}/(1-\beta)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\text{Perturbation}_{a}|=|\beta(1-\beta)d_{k-1}|=\beta(1-\beta)|d_{k-1}|\leq\beta(1-\beta)q|a_{k-1}|=\beta(1-\beta)q\frac{|a^{\prime}_{k-1}|}{1-\beta}=\beta q|a^{\prime}_{k-1}|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mtext>Perturbation</mtext><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\text{Perturbation}_{a}|=|\beta(1-\beta)d_{k-1}|=\beta(1-\beta)|d_{k-1}|\leq\beta(1-\beta)q|a_{k-1}|=\beta(1-\beta)q\frac{|a^{\prime}_{k-1}|}{1-\beta}=\beta q|a^{\prime}_{k-1}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conclusion of Proof.<span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Both systems, <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{c_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{c_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and the scaled <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{a^{\prime}_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{a^{\prime}_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, adhere to the same mathematical dynamics. Their evolution is governed by an identical recurrence structure, and their respective perturbation terms are bounded by the exact same relative factor <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta q</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to their own previous state. Therefore, from an analytical standpoint, the two systems are indistinguishable. Any conclusion regarding the long-term behavior (e.g., convergence, stability) of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{c_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{c_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> under its perturbation model will apply directly to <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{a^{\prime}_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{a^{\prime}_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> (and thus proportionally to <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{a_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{a_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>) under its own perturbation model.
∎</span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">With Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1 (Equivalence of Perturbed Dynamical Systems). ‣ Equivalence of Quantization Schemes. ‣ A.1 Preliminaries ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem ‣ A Convergence Analysis of Adaptive Optimizers under Floating-point Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> established, we can now apply this general result to our specific case of Quantized Adam. The weighted-sum moment <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{m}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{m}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> from our analysis corresponds to the abstract sequence <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{a_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{a_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, while the standard weighted-average moment <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{m}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{m}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{c_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{c_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The gradient term <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{g}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{g}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{b_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{b_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the relative quantization errors in both schemes are modeled by the perturbations <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{d_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{d_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{e_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{e_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> with the bound factor <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1 (Equivalence of Perturbed Dynamical Systems). ‣ Equivalence of Quantization Schemes. ‣ A.1 Preliminaries ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem ‣ A Convergence Analysis of Adaptive Optimizers under Floating-point Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> thus formally proves that analyzing the quantization of our weighted-sum moment <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{m}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{m}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is analytically equivalent to analyzing the quantization of the standard weighted-average moment <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{m}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{m}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. This rigorously justifies our proof strategy and ensures that our theoretical findings are directly relevant to practical implementations of Quantized Adam. A parallel argument holds for the second moments <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{v}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> with decay factor <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Detailed Proof</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To systematically analyze the effects of quantization, we begin by isolating the different sources of error. We introduce auxiliary moment estimates, <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\prime}_{t,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\prime}_{t,i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\prime}_{t,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\prime}_{t,i}</annotation></semantics></math>, which are defined to incorporate the quantization error from the stochastic gradient, <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{t,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{t,i}</annotation></semantics></math>, but are themselves assumed to be stored with perfect precision. Their dynamics are given by:</p>
<table id="A1.E7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E7X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle m^{\prime}_{t,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle m^{\prime}_{t,i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta_{1}m^{\prime}_{t-1,i}+(\nabla_{i}f_{t}(\mathbf{w}_{t-1})+\delta_{t,i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta_{1}m^{\prime}_{t-1,i}+(\nabla_{i}f_{t}(\mathbf{w}_{t-1})+\delta_{t,i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(A.7)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E7Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v^{\prime}_{t,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v^{\prime}_{t,i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta_{2}v^{\prime}_{t-1,i}+(\nabla_{i}f_{t}(\mathbf{w}_{t-1})+\delta_{t,i})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta_{2}v^{\prime}_{t-1,i}+(\nabla_{i}f_{t}(\mathbf{w}_{t-1})+\delta_{t,i})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Throughout the following proof we note <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{t-1}\left[\cdot\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{t-1}\left[\cdot\right]</annotation></semantics></math> the conditional expectation with respect to <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{1},\ldots,f_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{1},\ldots,f_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is deterministic knowing <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{1},\ldots,f_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{1},\ldots,f_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
With slightly abuse of notation in the detailed proof, We introduce</p>
<table id="A1.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{t}=\nabla F(\mathbf{w}_{t-1})\quad\text{and}\quad\mathbf{g}_{t}=\nabla f_{t}(\mathbf{w}_{t-1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{t}=\nabla F(\mathbf{w}_{t-1})\quad\text{and}\quad\mathbf{g}_{t}=\nabla f_{t}(\mathbf{w}_{t-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We introduce the update <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, as well as the update without momentum <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t,i}=\frac{m_{t,i}}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v_{t,i}}}\quad\text{and}\quad U_{t,i}=\frac{g_{t,i}+\delta_{t,i}}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v^{\prime}_{t,i}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msqrt><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t,i}=\frac{m_{t,i}}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v_{t,i}}}\quad\text{and}\quad U_{t,i}=\frac{g_{t,i}+\delta_{t,i}}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v^{\prime}_{t,i}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&lt;t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&lt;t</annotation></semantics></math>, we define <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{v}_{t,k}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{v}_{t,k}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{v}_{t,k,i}=\beta_{2}^{k}v^{\prime}_{t-k,i}+\mathbb{E}_{t-k}\left[\sum_{j=t-k+1}^{t}\beta_{2}^{t-j}(g_{j,i}+\delta_{j,i})^{2}\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{v}_{t,k,i}=\beta_{2}^{k}v^{\prime}_{t-k,i}+\mathbb{E}_{t-k}\left[\sum_{j=t-k+1}^{t}\beta_{2}^{t-j}(g_{j,i}+\delta_{j,i})^{2}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">i.e. the contribution from the <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> last gradients are replaced by their expected value for know values of <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{1},\ldots,f_{t-k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{1},\ldots,f_{t-k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Using the smoothness of <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F(\mathbf{w}_{t})\leq F(\mathbf{w}_{t-1})-\eta_{t}\mathcal{G}_{t}^{T}\mathbf{u}_{t}+\frac{\eta_{t}^{2}L}{2}\|\mathbf{u}_{t}\|^{2}_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F(\mathbf{w}_{t})\leq F(\mathbf{w}_{t-1})-\eta_{t}\mathcal{G}_{t}^{T}\mathbf{u}_{t}+\frac{\eta_{t}^{2}L}{2}\|\mathbf{u}_{t}\|^{2}_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The overall motivation of our proof is to find a lower bound for <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{t}\mathcal{G}_{t}^{T}\mathbf{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{t}\mathcal{G}_{t}^{T}\mathbf{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{G}_{t}^{T}\mathbf{u}_{t}=\sum_{i\in[d]}\mathcal{G}_{t,i}\frac{m_{t,i}}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v_{t,i}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msqrt><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{G}_{t}^{T}\mathbf{u}_{t}=\sum_{i\in[d]}\mathcal{G}_{t,i}\frac{m_{t,i}}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v_{t,i}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We can rewrite <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{t}^{T}\mathbf{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{t}^{T}\mathbf{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> as:</p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i\in[d]}\mathcal{G}_{t,i}\frac{m_{t,i}}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v_{t,i}}}=\underbrace{(\sum_{i\in[d]}\mathcal{G}_{t,i}\frac{m_{t,i}}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v_{t,i}}}-\sum_{i\in[d]}\mathcal{G}_{t,i}\frac{m^{\prime}_{t,i}}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v^{\prime}_{t,i}}})}_{A}+\underbrace{\sum_{i\in[d]}\mathcal{G}_{t,i}\frac{m^{\prime}_{t,i}}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v^{\prime}_{t,i}}}}_{B}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msqrt><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msqrt><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msqrt><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mi>A</mi></munder><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msqrt><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mi>B</mi></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i\in[d]}\mathcal{G}_{t,i}\frac{m_{t,i}}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v_{t,i}}}=\underbrace{(\sum_{i\in[d]}\mathcal{G}_{t,i}\frac{m_{t,i}}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v_{t,i}}}-\sum_{i\in[d]}\mathcal{G}_{t,i}\frac{m^{\prime}_{t,i}}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v^{\prime}_{t,i}}})}_{A}+\underbrace{\sum_{i\in[d]}\mathcal{G}_{t,i}\frac{m^{\prime}_{t,i}}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v^{\prime}_{t,i}}}}_{B}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Here, Term A represents the error component arising from the quantization of the momentum accumulators (<math id="A1.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{m}_{t},\mathbf{v}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{m}_{t},\mathbf{v}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>), while Term B represents the behavior of the update driven by an ideal accumulator.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Now we can bound term A. We split A into two parts as before:</p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A|\leq\underbrace{\left|\sum_{i\in[d]}\mathcal{G}_{t,i}\frac{m_{t,i}-m^{\prime}_{t,i}}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v_{t,i}}}\right|}_{A_{1}}+\underbrace{\left|\sum_{i\in[d]}\mathcal{G}_{t,i}\left(\frac{m^{\prime}_{t,i}}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v_{t,i}}}-\frac{m^{\prime}_{t,i}}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v^{\prime}_{t,i}}}\right)\right|}_{A_{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msqrt><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msqrt><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A|\leq\underbrace{\left|\sum_{i\in[d]}\mathcal{G}_{t,i}\frac{m_{t,i}-m^{\prime}_{t,i}}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v_{t,i}}}\right|}_{A_{1}}+\underbrace{\left|\sum_{i\in[d]}\mathcal{G}_{t,i}\left(\frac{m^{\prime}_{t,i}}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v_{t,i}}}-\frac{m^{\prime}_{t,i}}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v^{\prime}_{t,i}}}\right)\right|}_{A_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">The first term, <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, which arises from the quantization noise on the first moment <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐦</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, is bounded using Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma A.3 (Bound on Discrete Error). ‣ A.4 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem ‣ A Convergence Analysis of Adaptive Optimizers under Floating-point Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a> (with <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=q_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=q_{M}</annotation></semantics></math>) and Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma A.5 (Bound on the Quantized Momentum Error Ratio). ‣ A.6 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem ‣ A Convergence Analysis of Adaptive Optimizers under Floating-point Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|A_{1}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|A_{1}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{i\in[d]}R\frac{|m_{t,i}-m^{\prime}_{t,i}|}{\sqrt{v_{t,i}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{i\in[d]}R\frac{|m_{t,i}-m^{\prime}_{t,i}|}{\sqrt{v_{t,i}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq R\sum_{i\in[d]}\frac{\sum_{k=0}^{t}(\beta_{1}^{t-k}((1+q_{M})^{t-k}-1))|\nabla_{i}f_{k}(\mathbf{w}_{k-1})+\delta_{k,i}|}{\sqrt{\sum_{k=0}^{t}\beta_{2}^{t-k}(1-q_{V})^{t-k}(\nabla_{i}f_{k}(\mathbf{w}_{k-1})+\delta_{k,i})^{2}}}\leq q_{M}\cdot dR\cdot C_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq R\sum_{i\in[d]}\frac{\sum_{k=0}^{t}(\beta_{1}^{t-k}((1+q_{M})^{t-k}-1))|\nabla_{i}f_{k}(\mathbf{w}_{k-1})+\delta_{k,i}|}{\sqrt{\sum_{k=0}^{t}\beta_{2}^{t-k}(1-q_{V})^{t-k}(\nabla_{i}f_{k}(\mathbf{w}_{k-1})+\delta_{k,i})^{2}}}\leq q_{M}\cdot dR\cdot C_{q}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{q}=\frac{\sqrt{r^{\prime}(1+r^{\prime})}}{(1+q_{M})(1-r^{\prime})^{3/2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{q}=\frac{\sqrt{r^{\prime}(1+r^{\prime})}}{(1+q_{M})(1-r^{\prime})^{3/2}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\prime}=\frac{\beta_{1}^{2}(1+q_{M})^{2}}{\beta_{2}(1-q_{V})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}=\frac{\beta_{1}^{2}(1+q_{M})^{2}}{\beta_{2}(1-q_{V})}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">For the second term, <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we use the bound on the gradient <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathcal{G}_{t}\|_{\infty}\leq R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathcal{G}_{t}\|_{\infty}\leq R</annotation></semantics></math> and apply Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma A.2 (The value range of 𝑣_{𝑡,𝑖} and the upper bound of |{1/√{ϵ+𝑣_{𝑡,𝑖}}}-{1/√{ϵ+𝑣^′_{𝑡,𝑖}}}|). ‣ A.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem ‣ A Convergence Analysis of Adaptive Optimizers under Floating-point Quantization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>, which requires a case analysis.</p>
<table id="A1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|A_{2}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|A_{2}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{i\in[d]}R|m^{\prime}_{t,i}|\left|\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v_{t,i}}}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v^{\prime}_{t,i}}}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{i\in[d]}R|m^{\prime}_{t,i}|\left|\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v_{t,i}}}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v^{\prime}_{t,i}}}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{i\in[d]}R|m^{\prime}_{t,i}|\max\left\{\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon+LB_{t,i}}}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v^{\prime}_{t,i}}},\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v^{\prime}_{t,i}}}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon+UB_{t,i}}}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{i\in[d]}R|m^{\prime}_{t,i}|\max\left\{\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon+LB_{t,i}}}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v^{\prime}_{t,i}}},\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v^{\prime}_{t,i}}}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon+UB_{t,i}}}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{k,i}=\nabla_{i}f_{k}(\mathbf{w}_{k-1})+\delta_{k,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{k,i}=\nabla_{i}f_{k}(\mathbf{w}_{k-1})+\delta_{k,i}</annotation></semantics></math>. We analyze the two terms inside the <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>max</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max</annotation></semantics></math> for a single coordinate <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case I (Deviation from Lower Bound):</span> Following the approximation in the provided sketch, we have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|m^{\prime}_{t,i}|\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon+LB_{t,i}}}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v^{\prime}_{t,i}}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|m^{\prime}_{t,i}|\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon+LB_{t,i}}}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v^{\prime}_{t,i}}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=|m^{\prime}_{t,i}|\left(\frac{v^{\prime}_{t,i}-LB_{t,i}}{\sqrt{\epsilon+LB_{t,i}}\sqrt{\epsilon+v^{\prime}_{t,i}}(\sqrt{\epsilon+LB_{t,i}}+\sqrt{\epsilon+v^{\prime}_{t,i}})}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=|m^{\prime}_{t,i}|\left(\frac{v^{\prime}_{t,i}-LB_{t,i}}{\sqrt{\epsilon+LB_{t,i}}\sqrt{\epsilon+v^{\prime}_{t,i}}(\sqrt{\epsilon+LB_{t,i}}+\sqrt{\epsilon+v^{\prime}_{t,i}})}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{|m^{\prime}_{t,i}|}{\sqrt{\epsilon+LB_{t,i}}}\frac{v^{\prime}_{t,i}-LB_{t,i}}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v^{\prime}_{t,i}}(\sqrt{\epsilon+LB_{t,i}}+\sqrt{\epsilon+v^{\prime}_{t,i}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{|m^{\prime}_{t,i}|}{\sqrt{\epsilon+LB_{t,i}}}\frac{v^{\prime}_{t,i}-LB_{t,i}}{\sqrt{\epsilon+v^{\prime}_{t,i}}(\sqrt{\epsilon+LB_{t,i}}+\sqrt{\epsilon+v^{\prime}_{t,i}})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
